Open-shell relativistic calculations on the Boron atom
=======================================================

We seek to get the first excited state, 2P_3/2, of B (X 2P_1/2), and
find out 2P1/2-2P3/2 fine structure splitting.

We selected the Dirac-Coulomb Hamiltonian with neglected (SS|SS) class of integrals.

== Complete open-shell CI

One way to get the value is performing small CI over the active open-shell space, 6 2p orbitals,
which are splittend.

For pedagogical purposes we have 
employed several computational symmetries.

Starting from the average SCF occupation (one electron distributed over 2p1/2 and 2p3/2 shells), 

../../../pam -noarch B.sto-3g.lsym.mol B.2Pav.dc_rkb.scf_2fs_cosci.inp
../../../pam -noarch B.sto-3g.D2h.mol B.2Pav.dc_rkb.scf_2fs_cosci.inp

for one-fermion symmetries,

../../../pam -noarch B.sto-3g.C2v.mol B.2Pav.dc_rkb.scf_1fs_cosci.inp
../../../pam -noarch B.sto-3g.C1.mol B.2Pav.dc_rkb.scf_1fs_cosci.inp

we get the value of 17.179488 cm-1 and in the outputs we see the proper degeneracy
of resulting total CI energies - 2 and 4. 

(By averaging COSCI energies we get SCF energy of the average occupation;

((2*(-24.249116730099) + 4*(-24.249038454591)))/6 = -24.249064546427
                                    SCF energy:     -24.249064546425263


== MO reordering 

First one has to obtain the MO coefficients file of the ground state:

../../../pam -noarch -utcmo B.sto-3g.D2h.mol B.2P12.dc_rkb.scf_2fs.inp
../../../pam -noarch -utcmo B.sto-3g.C1.mol  B.2P12.dc_rkb.scf_1fs.inp

and use them for calculation of the excited state:

../../../pam -noarch -incmo B.sto-3g.D2h.mol  B.2P32.dc_rkb.scf_2fs_reord_ovlsel.inp
../../../pam -incmo -noarch B.sto-3g.C1.mol   B.2P32.dc_rkb.scf_1fs_reord_ovlsel.inp


For the linear symmetry one can utilize M_J specified occupation of shells both for ground
and first excited state. Only the preDHF reordering works, not the overlap selection !

../../../pam -noarch -utcmo B.sto-3g.lsym.mol B.2P12.dc_rkb.scf_2fs_mj.inp
../../../pam -noarch -incmo B.sto-3g.lsym.mol B.2P32.dc_rkb.scf_2fs_reord_mj.inp

Finally, in the output one can see proper order of spinors for the excited state - first 2p3/2 spinors 
(four-fold degeneracy),
and then the 2p1/2 spinors (two-fold degeneracy):

* Fermion symmetry E1u
  * Open shell #1, f = 0.2500
 -0.28691011961454  ( 4)
  * Virtual eigenvalues, f = 0.0000
  0.12724113329935  ( 2)

SCF energy 2_P_1/2: -24.249116730391307
SCF energy 2_P_3/2: -24.249038454664991
FSS : (-24.249116730391307+24.249038454664991)*219474.631280634 cm-1 = 17.179536 cm-1
what is close to the above given COSCI value of  17.179488 cm-1.

== Correlated calculations ==

== Conclusions ==
Further quality improvement of the theoretical data 
 would be in enlarging basis set. The current one, decontracted STO-3G,
is small and is chosen for demonstrative purposes only.

